# Architecture standard

{% if profile == "minimal" -%}
Keep the minimal profile direct: `main.py` owns the small public behavior. Do not introduce domain,
application, or adapter layers until a concrete feature needs a stable boundary.
{% elif profile == "application" -%}
Preserve `main`/bootstrap → application → domain. The domain must not import application code,
configuration, frameworks, or infrastructure. Bootstrap is the composition root; configuration is
read at that boundary and passed inward explicitly.
{% else -%}
Preserve entrypoint/bootstrap → application → domain. Adapters may depend on application or
domain contracts, never the reverse. Bootstrap selects and wires concrete adapters; keep framework
and side-effect details at those outer boundaries.
{% endif %}

Create packages for clear ownership, not as speculative placeholders. Do not add generic buckets
such as `services`, `models`, `repositories`, `utils`, `helpers`, or `data`.
